Subject: [PATCH 6.18.y 0/8] can: bcm: backport of 8 patches that failed to
 apply to 6.18-stable

This resubmits "can: bcm: add locking when updating filter and timer
values" (commit 749179c2e25b95d22499ed29096b3e02d6dfd2b4 upstream),
which failed to apply to the 6.18-stable tree, together with 7
further bcm.c patches from the same upstream series that build on it
and would otherwise fail for the same reason. This is the full set
of 11 upstream bcm.c patches from 7.2-rc3 minus the 3 already queued
by the normal stable process for 6.18 ("can: bcm: defer rx_op
deallocation to workqueue to fix thrtimer UAF", "can: bcm: fix
lockless bound/ifindex race and silent RX_SETUP failure", "can: bcm:
add missing rcu list annotations and operations").

As on 6.12.y, none of these 8 patches needed content adaptation for
the traffic_flags/RX_LOCAL/RX_OWN context: 6.18-stable already
carries commit fec846fa7eddf7bb651bf88bd78c7db1410ae3b1 ("can: bcm:
add recvmsg flags for own, local and remote traffic", Jan 2024) as
part of its own baseline. All 8 patches apply cleanly once the 3
already-queued patches are in place; they were previously reported
as FAILED for that missing-prerequisite reason alone, not for
independent conflicts.

Patch 5/8 ("add missing device refcount for CAN filter removal") is
the one exception: upstream uses the netdevice_tracker/netdev_hold()/
netdev_put() debug-tracking infra. Out of caution this series
replaces it with the plain, always-available dev_hold()/dev_put(),
which is functionally identical for the actual fix (holding a
reference across a concurrent NETDEV_UNREGISTER) - just without the
extra leak-tracking instrumentation. This mirrors the same adaptation
made on the other branches in this series after an actual build
failure was reported on 5.10.y ("error: unknown type name
'netdevice_tracker'"); this revision has been verified with a clean
git am against a seeded net/can/bcm.c and no longer references that
type anywhere in the result.

This assumes the 3 already-queued bcm.c patches for 6.18-stable have
landed by the time this is applied. If not, please let me know and I
will rebase.

Oliver Hartkopp (8):
  can: bcm: add locking when updating filter and timer values
  can: bcm: fix CAN frame rx/tx statistics
  can: bcm: extend bcm_tx_lock usage for data and timer updates
  can: bcm: validate frame length in bcm_rx_setup() for RTR replies
  can: bcm: add missing device refcount for CAN filter removal
  can: bcm: fix stale rx/tx ops after device removal
  can: bcm: fix data race on rx_stamp/rx_ifindex in bcm_rx_handler()
  can: bcm: track a single source interface for ANYDEV timeout/throttle
    ops

